                                                    <div class="body-medium text-indent text-color-clay w-richtext">
                                                        <p>Alexandria helps clients move from uncertainty to clarity on federal and state tax issues. Her work centers on clean analysis, timely filings, and positions that stand up to scrutiny. She joined
                                                            the firm as an intern in January of 2024. After passing the Illinois Bar that same year, she quickly became a steady partner to clients navigating multi-stakeholder matters, cross-jurisdictional
                                                            rules, IRS examinations and litigation, transaction design, and compliance matters. At Chicago-Kent, she served as a Vice President of the Student Bar Association; earlier studies in History,
                                                            Spanish, and Leadership sharpen the way she listens, frames issues, and translates rules into actionable next steps.</p>
